From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:47:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 55/56] test: browser tests reach app modules through the
 fixture page, and follow v0.15's frame markup

v0.15 serves the browser fixtures as a production build (vite preview), so a
page can no longer import('/src/...') itself. The fixtures now list the app
modules our tests drive (store, liveFrames, gpuPictures, gpuLabels,
renderTrialClient) and expose them as window.testImport(path): the same
module instances the page uses.

The rest follow upstream's markup and our own first load:
- a frame's iframe now sits in a bleed wrapper, so its picture is found
  from the grandparent (zoomPictures, liveFrames);
- the paper grid is [data-pixel-grid="paper"] (stageGrid);
- the first load mounts a frame's document only after the labels (0048),
  so pageCanvas waits for the iframe before counting;
- frameEdge zooms to 0.1-0.29, where culling shows pictures: it turns
  culling off to look at live documents.
